# Deploy after production work

When TrustID changes are production-ready (features, UX, fixes the user can use live):

1. Commit with a clear message (follow the repo git safety protocol).
2. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`main` unless told otherwise).
3. Confirm Netlify auto-deploy for `trustedid` when the push is to `main` (site: https://trustedid.netlify.app).
4. Do this without waiting to be asked again — the user prefers automatic GitHub + Netlify after every production change.

Do not push WIP experiments, secrets, or `*.tsbuildinfo` / build artifacts unless they are intentionally tracked.
